The implementation is complete and all tests pass. Here's what was added to `src/store.rs`:

```rust
pub fn rename(dir: &Path, old_id: &str, new_id: &str, new_title: &str) -> std::io::Result<()>
```

**How it works:**

1. Reads the note file at `{old_id}.note`.
2. Splits the content on `SEP` (the `\n---\n` delimiter) into 4 parts: id, title, pinned flag, body.
3. Validates that the file exists and the stored id matches `old_id` (returns `NotFound` otherwise).
4. Reconstructs the content with `new_id` and `new_title`, keeping the existing pinned flag and body (and thus tags) intact.
5. Writes the new file as `{new_id}.note`.
6. Deletes the old file, so no trace remains under `old_id`.

After `rename`, a subsequent `load_all(dir)` will return exactly one note with the new id and title.


